Axis signs and slides: PRECOMPUTED and VERIFIED here, not enumerated (EXO-218). The solve is `sweepgen.solve_axis_signs` - pure Python, deterministic, no Fusion - and on this arm it is 2^5 combinations x four slide candidates each, hours of router calls. It was run by that function outside Fusion; this build checks the answer. All 32 combinations were tried (k = 5). 25 of them route all six links; this one has the shortest total centre line, 625.710 mm - the rule of `solve_axis_signs`, unchanged. Total slide 180.502 mm. R6 and R7 do not change the answer (k = 5 / 13 / 21 / 29 tie on every number), so the rule's last tie-break, the lowest combination, takes k = 5.
